      ["Cause", "Blood flukes, Schistosoma; 3 species: S. haematobium, S. mansoni, S. japonicum."],
      ["Endemic in the Philippines", "S. japonicum (Leyte, Samar, Sorsogon, Mindoro, Bohol)."],
      ["Intermediate host", "Oncomelania quadrasi (snail)."],
      ["Diagnosis", "Schistosoma eggs in stool; rectal biopsy; Kato-Katz; ultrasound of the hepatobiliary tract (HBT)."],
      ["Clinical manifestations", "Severe jaundice, edema, ascites, hepatosplenomegaly, signs and symptoms of portal hypertension."],
      ["Management", "Praziquantel 60 mg/kg single dose; supportive and symptomatic care."],
      ["Methods of control", "Educate the public on transmission and protection; proper disposal of feces and urine; prevent exposure to contaminated water; after accidental water exposure, towel dry and apply 70% alcohol to minimize penetration."],
      ["Points for control (life cycle)", "Contamination of water: health education, improved sanitation, drug treatment to reduce egg excretion. Intermediate host: molluscicides, elimination of habitats. Human contact with infection: health education, access to safe water supply."]
